  "conclusions": [
    "NVIDIA CUDA EULA text (11 replacement packages) and the NVIDIA SDK licence agreement (cuDNN) are byte-identical to the texts covered by assessment001; the cu12->cu13 builds keep the same NVIDIA use restrictions.",
    "nvidia-nccl BSD-3-Clause text differs from the assessed one only in its copyright year range (2015-2019 -> 2015-2020) and an added paragraph noting bundled NVTX files (github.com/NVIDIA/NVTX); still BSD-3-Clause.",
    "New packages cuda-bindings, cuda-pathfinder and nvidia-nvtx are Apache-2.0; cuda-toolkit is a metadata-only meta-package with no installed payload or licence file.",
    "torch 2.14.1 declares Apache-2.0 AND Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception AND BSD-2-Clause AND BSD-3-Clause AND BSL-1.0 AND MIT and ships its bundled third-party notices; all permissive. Triton 3.8.0 is MIT. sympy, filelock, torchvision keep their licences.",
    "No copyleft or non-commercial licence enters the closure; the local-inference and output-use conclusions of assessment001 are unchanged. Notice preservation and NVIDIA restrictions continue to apply; redistribution remains unassessed."
  ],
  "primary_sources": [
    "https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/v2.14.1/LICENSE",
    "https://github.com/triton-lang/triton/blob/v3.8.0/LICENSE",
    "https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/eula/index.html",
    "https://github.com/NVIDIA/cuda-python/blob/main/LICENSE"
  ],
  "torch_bundled_notice_scan": {
    "files": 86,
    "classification": {
      "Apache-2.0": 13,
      "Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception": 5,
      "BSL-1.0/MIT": 1,
      "BSD": 19,
      "BSD-style redistribution": 22,
      "MIT": 26
    },
    "copyleft_or_noncommercial_matches": 0,
    "method": "First 3000 bytes keyword classification of every LICENSE/COPYING/NOTICE file in the torch dist-info. Full-text grep for GPL/LGPL/MPL/non-commercial hits 5 files, all \"GPLv2\" mentions inside Apache-2.0 LLVM-exception compatibility clauses (llvm-openmp and NVTX notices), not grants."
  },
  "additional_notes": [
    "sympy-1.14.0 licenses/AUTHORS is a novel contributor list, not a licence.",
    "torch/_vendor/quack/LICENSE (outside dist-info) is Apache-2.0.",
    "nvidia-cusparselt-cu13 ships no licence file, as the assessed cu12 wheel did not.",
    "nvidia-nvtx ships Apache-2.0 text although its classifier says Other/Proprietary; the assessed nvtx-cu12 shipped the NVIDIA EULA."
  ]
